From 954ecf7dd81be4f1eadf87de59c3ee35398c944e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:48:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Worker pickup: machine-pinned cards first; never
 copy a pre-claim pin-walled card

worker-1 2026-11-14 (t_01a1d8ad896977b9 -> root fix t_01a1d95eabbd2b9d): t_01a1d6d855a058a2
(runs_on machine:worker-1) waited `budget_exhausted` ~6 h (03:33Z-09:22Z) while the pickup copied
t_01a1d882f58d9df9 ~700 times (every ~18 s).

Five whys:
1. Why did the pinned card wait? Every pickup batch was full before it was reached.
2. Why full? (a) t_01a1d882f58d9df9, a fresh require_model card pinned to quota-walled
   openai-codex/gpt-6-astra, was copied each tick; (b) pool cards were ranked ahead of it.
3. Why copied each tick? Local dispatch holds it `pinned_quota_wall` pre-claim, eviction drops
   the held copy, and `_quota_held` only predicted holds for cards WITH a quota episode. A card
   that never ran has none, so the prediction returned None.
4. Why pool cards first? `_evaluate` ordered each lane by `order_with_remote_waiters` only; a
   card pinned to this machine had no precedence over cards any pool worker can take.
5. Why not caught? The t_01a1cf9f2b838cbb fix covered only the post-run episode hold.

Fix (hermes_cli/kanban_worker_node.py):
- `_quota_held`: with no episode, predict the pre-claim hold with the dispatcher's own
  read-only `kanban_dispatch_skip.pinned_quota_hold` on the replica (ready lane only, as
  `hold_pinned_quota`). Such a card is not copied, spends no budget, and records
  `quota_hold` "pinned_quota_wall <model> (<provider>) until <reset>Z" (the pickup-stall
  detector's deadline parser reads it). Failures copy as before.
- `_evaluate`: within each lane, cards pinned to this machine (`mine`) go first; a stable
  sort keeps each group's existing order. Review still precedes ready.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pickup_pinned_first.py), RED on base 7300ceed9f, GREEN here:
- a mandatory pin on a walled model with no episode is not copied (budget 1 starts the pinned
  card; no churn over 3 more ticks; skip reason quota_hold), with dispatcher parity asserted;
- the same pin with no wall is copied;
- budget 2 with 3 higher-priority pool cards: the machine-pinned card is picked first.

test_kanban_pickup_held_budget.py: two tests encoded the old order (a pool card ahead of a card
pinned here); they now pin the competing card too or give the budget room, keeping their intent
(free held copies bounded by FREE_PER_TICK; an unreadable Board hold takes the budget).
All 123 test files importing kanban_worker_node / kanban_dispatch_skip / kanban_pickup pass.
